<title>USA: Keithley Q1 Dec 31 turns to loss.</title>
<headline>Keithley Q1 Dec 31 turns to loss.</headline>
<dateline>CLEVELAND 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>KEITHLEY INSTRUMENTS INC</p>
<p> 3 MONTHS ENDED DEC 31,     1996		   1995</p>
<p> NET SALES		   $27,886		 $29,823</p>
<p> COST OF GOODS SOLD	 11,754		  11,835</p>
<p> NET INCOME (LOSS)	   (838)		   1,145</p>
<p> NET EPS			 (.11)		     .15</p>
<p> WGTD AVG SHRS (000)	 7,473		   7,834</p>
<p>	    (In Thousands of Dollars Except for Per Share Data)</p>
<p>NOTE: The company reported sales declines in all divisions except the Instruments division, which experienced a slight increase from prior year's levels.</p>
<p>Sales of the company's parametric test systems serving the semiconductor industry were down significantly from the level of a year ago.</p>
<p>The company previously announced that it expected the fiscal 1997 first quarter loss to be in the $.11 to $.12 per share range.</p>
</text>
